# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository-root ignores.
#
# Backend/.gitignore covers the application tree. This file covers the
# repository root, which previously had no .gitignore at all - that is how
# deploy-secrets/ and the pasted Postgres credentials reached a public remote.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Key material. Never commit a private key; deployed environments read it from
# their own secret store (see docs/RENDER_DEPLOYMENT.md).
deploy-secrets/
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
firebase-service-account*.json
service-account*.json

# Credentials pasted out of a provider dashboard for convenience.
*credentials*.txt
*secret*.txt
*password*.txt
postgres*details*.txt
postgress*details*.txt

# Environments
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build artefacts that do not belong in version control
*.zip

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
